  "description": "Actian NoSQL, formerly the Versant Object Database, is a transactional object database that stores C++, Java and .NET object graphs directly, with online schema evolution, distributed multi-database transactions and high-availability options. It has a long history in telecom network management, defence and transport systems where object models are deep and latency matters. Actian (now part of HCLSoftware) still sells it alongside the embeddable FastObjects edition and now ships Docker images and a Kubernetes operator. It is a legacy-but-supported choice: dependable for existing installations, rarely chosen for greenfield work.",
